  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gomal Zam Dam Command Area Development Project (GZD-CADP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Gomal Zam Dam Command Area Development Project (GZD-CADP) is USAID&apos;s Government to Government (G2G) activity with the Government of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa (GoKP). USAID and the GoKP signed the Activity Agreement on March 18, 2015 for agriculture development of 191,000 acres (77,295 hectares) in the districts of Dera Ismail Khan and Tank. The main objective of the GZD-CADP is to ensure that the water available for the Gomal Zam command area is used efficiently through integrated development of the command area and farm water management, among other technical assistance components that will enhance agricultural productivity. The project will build the physical system and train operators on modern farming irrigation systems. An estimated 30,000 families will directly benefit from development of the command area.</narrative>
  </description>
